SUMMARY:There Will Be Blood (2007)
LOCATION:The Marquee\, Union South
DESCRIPTION:US | 158 min | R | Dir. Paul Thomas Anderson\n \n \n\n"Silve
 r miner Daniel Plainview (Daniel Day-Lewis) leads a hardscrabble life wit
 h his son\, H.W. (Dillon Freasier). When he hears about oil oozing from t
 he ground near the Western town of Little Boston\, Daniel takes his son o
 n a mission to find their fortune. Daniel makes his lucky strike and beco
 mes a self-made tycoon but\, as his fortune grows\, he deviates into mora
 l bankruptcy." - Rotten Tomatoes\n \n \n \n"The film is above all a co
 nsummate work of art\, one that transcends the historically fraught conte
 xt of its making\, and its pleasures are unapologetically aesthetic. It r
 eveals\, excites\, disturbs\, provokes\, but the window it opens is to hu
 man consciousness itself."        - Manohla Dargis for New York Times
 \n \n\n \n \n \nWatch the trailer here: https://www.youtube.com/watch
 ?v=FeSLPELpMeM \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n \n \nFor i
 nformation on available assistive content for WUD Film screenings\, pleas
 e visit the Assistive Movie Screenings in the Marquee Theater page.  \n
 Visit our Informed Moviegoing Resources page for links to resources that 
 explore film ratings and content alerts.\nThis event is intended for UW-M
 adison students\, faculty\, staff\, Wisconsin Union members and their gue
 sts. Anyone can become a Wisconsin Union member.\n\nhttps://union.wisc.ed
 u/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-film-presents-there-will
 -be-blood-2007\n\nSource: WUD Film (The Marquee)
URL:https://union.wisc.edu/events-and-activities/event-calendar/event/wud-
 film-presents-there-will-be-blood-2007
